; ============================================================
; String-Store-Test  —  read 3 lines, keep them, print them back
; ============================================================
; Needs Firmware-Math/GETSTR-2frag.dlines.txt flashed (uses $C2 GETSTR).
;
; Demonstrates the storage pattern:
;   $C2 GETSTR   reads a line into a buffer
;   $3B COPYMXMY copies the buffer into a numbered slot (block memory move)
;   $52 ADDXI    steps the slot pointer on by the slot size
;   $C1 PRINTSTR prints any slot back later, in any order
;
; Layout inside VM1's 4 KB block (addresses are program-relative; $09xx -> $49xx):
;   $0900   line buffer, 32 bytes      (working area, reused each line)
;   $0A00   slot 0  \
;   $0A20   slot 1   >  32 bytes each
;   $0A40   slot 2  /
;
; Type three lines. It then prints them back as slot2, slot0, slot1 to show the
; slots are independently addressable, not just a stream.
;
; Expected (typing ALPHA, BETA, GAMMA):
;   ALPHABETAGAMMA        <- the echo as you type
;   GAMMA
;   ALPHA
;   BETA
;
; The loop uses $B5 LOOPI (the ADDRESS form), but $B6 LOOPL (the LABEL form)
; works here too - both were tested on a cold-booted VM and give the same result.
;
; CORRECTION, for the record: an earlier version of this comment claimed LOOPL
; was broken. That was wrong. The apparent failure was a test-harness artifact -
; the harness started execution straight at $4000 without the VM launch that runs
; the label pre-pass, so the label table at $3200 was still empty on the first
; pass. GTL then took its undefined-label error path, the VM restarted, the
; pre-pass ran, and the retry worked - which looked like an erratic branch back
; to $4000. On a properly booted VM the pre-pass populates the table first and
; LOOPL is correct.
; ============================================================

; ---- CODE ($4000..$4058) ----
D 4000 CD
D 4001 11 03 0A 00
D 4005 11 05 00 03
D 4009 11 06 00 00
D 400D 11 01 09 00
D 4011 11 02 09 00
D 4015 C2 12
D 4017 3B 23 20
D 401A 52 03 00 20
D 401E 42 06
D 4020 B5 65 00 0D
D 4024 10 00 0D C9
D 4028 10 00 0A C9
D 402C 11 03 0A 40
D 4030 C1 03
D 4032 10 00 0D C9
D 4036 10 00 0A C9
D 403A 11 03 0A 00
D 403E C1 03
D 4040 10 00 0D C9
D 4044 10 00 0A C9
D 4048 11 03 0A 20
D 404C C1 03
D 404E 10 00 0D C9
D 4052 10 00 0A C9
D 4056 F0 00 00
D 5000 00
D 6000 00
D 7000 00
